entries.summary:
Viewport picking. Obtain it from {ModraUp::View#pick_helper}. The same instance will be reused.
{#do_pick} / {#window_pick} / {#boundingbox_pick} record the pick results;
{#init} / {#test_point} / {#pick_segment} only test the screen aperture, unrelated to those records.

examples.code:
def declare_params_and_ui(args)
  { length: { type: 'length', label: 'Length', default: 120 } }.to_json
end

def get_widget_states(args)
  { gap: { enabled: args[:parameters][:count] > 1 } }
end

class TipTool
  def getMenu(menu)
    menu.add_item("Cancel") { ModraUp.active_model.select_tool(nil) }
  end
end

entries.summary:
Register {ModraUp::ToolsObserver}. Adding the same object a second time returns +false+.
The cut tool dispatches +onActiveToolChanged(tools, tool_name, tool_id)+;
for a start state of 1 and end state of 0, the move/scale gesture dispatches +onToolStateChanged+.

